  "uprn": "200003993201",
  "decision_date": "22/06/2005",
  "description": "Change of use of each unit from office to one bed flats.",
  "site_name": "Westbourne House",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "07/06/2004",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": null,
  "street_name": null,
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major all other major developments",
  "lapsed_date": "21/06/2010",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - It is considered that the proposed change of use from offices to two one-bedroom self contained flats, because of their design, position and appearance, would be acceptable. The proposal would accord with the Councils Residential Standards and Controls, and would not harm neighbours' living conditions or local highway conditions. On balance, the development is in accordance with adopted Unitary Development Plan policies ENV-B.1.1, H.4.1, H.3.3 and IMP.2.2.  It is considered that where the development is not compliant there are no undue adverse effects resulting from this.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the extension hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building.",
    "Condition : 4 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is occupied.",
    "Condition : 5 - The flats hereby permitted shall not be occupied until full particulars and details of a scheme to insulate the premises against the transmission of airborne and impact sound between the floors and the internal walls of the existing and proposed flats has been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and the development shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given.",
    "Condition : 6 - The use hereby permitted shall not be begun until details of the arrangements for storing of waste and recycled materials have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The arrangements for storing waste and recycled materials shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given and shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 7 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of  08.00 to 18.00 on Mondays to Friday and 08.00 to 13.00 on Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and public holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority."
  ],
